{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Root verification confirmed Jira setup and adoption-template defects. The bridge setup command writes only Jira connection keys and runs an access check. A new projects mapping has an empty sync list until the operator runs rebar bridge projects set, but the setup recipe does not make that operation a required step. The copied GitHub workflows default BRIDGE_BOT_EMAIL to joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com, while the setup guide documents rebar-bridge@users.noreply.github.com. The workflow therefore embeds a project-specific identity in client templates. templates/rebar-usage.md and its generated AGENTS template list six relations, omit caused_by, and instruct an explicit assignee instead of explaining the configured default-assignee policy."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787297049260793001,"uuid":"05deb629-8d87-4614-9571-676b824d7b43"}